    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the forward fuselage frames between stations C36 and C44 on the passenger aircraft, covering the frame doublers, the lower webs, the upper cleats and the splice plate at station C40.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the forward fuselage frames between stations C36 and C44 on the passenger aircraft, including the structure that surrounds the forward cargo door cut-out.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 is the left-hand side viewed from inside the compartment; the right-hand side is symmetrically opposite and is not drawn separately. The splice plate at item 30 is fitted at station C40 only and is not present at the other stations. The item range 10 to 60 is closed: the numbering was laid out for the six detail parts of the passenger frame family and carries no spare positions between them."
    },
