    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the forward fuselage frames between stations C36 and C44, covering the frame doublers, the lower webs, the upper cleats and the splice plates around the cargo door cut-out.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the forward fuselage frames between stations C36 and C44, including the structure that surrounds the forward cargo door cut-out.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 is the left-hand side viewed from inside the compartment; sheet 2 shows the freighter differential at the same stations. The splice plate at item 40 is fitted at station C40 only and is not present at the other stations. Item 30 is the machined rib used on the freighter and is not interchangeable with the sheet-formed item on passenger aircraft. The freighter items could not be added at the end of the family without separating them from the frame details they belong with, so the family has been renumbered in one pass: the splice plate, the cleat, the rivet and the bolt move from items 30, 40, 50 and 60 to items 40, 50, 60 and 70. Orders raised against the earlier item numbers are still traceable through the part number."
    },
